From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <daryldenson0405@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] husky: keep app odex on /system, not system_other

BoardConfigMainlineCommon.mk turns on BOARD_USES_SYSTEM_OTHER_ODEX, which
moves the odex/vdex of every preopted app (SystemUIGoogle, SettingsGoogle,
LineageParts, ...) into system_other.img. Google's factory images flash that
image to the inactive slot and cppreopts copies it in on first boot; an
Evolution X zip or OTA never writes it, so those apps start every update
with no AOT code and SystemUI gestures hitch until background dexopt runs
(idle and charging, often overnight).

Build them into /system instead. This adds ~183 MB to the system
partitions, well inside the 8.5 GB super.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 husky/BoardConfig.mk | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/husky/BoardConfig.mk b/husky/BoardConfig.mk
index 5fcac28..f7c77e9 100644
--- a/husky/BoardConfig.mk
+++ b/husky/BoardConfig.mk
@@ -22,3 +22,10 @@ SYSTEM_EXT_PUBLIC_SEPOLICY_DIRS += \
 include $(DEVICE_PATH)/BoardConfigCommon.mk
 
 include $(VENDOR_PATH)/BoardConfigVendor.mk
+
+# Keep app odex on /system rather than system_other. Only a factory flash
+# writes system_other to the inactive slot; zip and OTA installs never do, so
+# SystemUIGoogle, SettingsGoogle and the other preopted priv-apps lose their
+# AOT code after every update and run interpreted/JIT until background
+# dexopt catches up (~183 MB, well inside super).
+BOARD_USES_SYSTEM_OTHER_ODEX :=
